# `node_modules/` is reproducible from the lockfile.
node_modules/

# pnpm's store, if a future `.npmrc` ever pins one inside the project.
.pnpm-store/

# Build output is committed on purpose: `lib/` is what the host loads, so a clone
# or a `github:` install works without a build step. Regenerate it with
# `pnpm run build` and commit the result alongside the source that produced it.
# `.gitattributes` marks it as generated so review tools fold it away.

# Maintainer-only release notes: they document this machine's workflow (registry
# mirror, remote layout, npm token handling) and are not part of the published
# plugin. Kept locally on purpose. `git add -f <file>` still stages them.
PUBLISHING.md
RELEASING.md

# Logs and caches.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editors.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Operating systems.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
